course: dictionary
lesson: 14818
title: The quatrain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A quatrain is a verse of four lines in a poem. A verse is a group of lines, and a quatrain is one kind of verse, so when you see a quatrain, count four lines.
explain: Look at the last word of each line to find the rhyme pattern. In «The sun is up, the sky is high, / The birds all sing and dart and fly, / The fields are green and stretch so wide, / The day is ours to try», the endings high and wide rhyme, and fly and try rhyme.
explain: Lines one and three share a rhyme, and lines two and four share a rhyme. This is an ABAB pattern. Another common pattern is AABB, where lines one and two rhyme, and lines three and four rhyme.
fact: A quatrain is a verse with four lines.
fact: Quatrains often follow a rhyme pattern such as ABAB or AABB.
fact: In ABAB, lines one and three rhyme, and lines two and four rhyme.
fact: Many nursery rhymes and hymns are built from quatrains, so you may already know some.
fact: Quatrain is a noun: one quatrain, two or more quatrains.
exercise: «The first quatrain of the poem has four lines.» How many lines are in a quatrain? | Fourteen | * Four | Six | Two
exercise: Lines one and three rhyme, and lines two and four rhyme. What is this rhyme pattern called? | AABB | AAAA | ABCD | * ABAB
exercise: Which of these is a quatrain? | * A four-line verse with a rhyme pattern like AABB | A poem with fourteen lines | A single line of a poem | A story told in one paragraph
test: «Her new poem has three quatrains, each with four lines.» How many lines are there in all three quatrains together? | * Twelve | Fourteen | Seven | Ten
test: Which rhyme pattern has lines one and two rhyming, and lines three and four rhyming? | ABAB | * AABB | ABBA | ABCD
exam: In a quatrain with an ABAB pattern, which lines must rhyme with each other? | * Lines one and three, and lines two and four | Lines one and four only | Lines one and two only | All four lines must end with the same word
